## Narrative
This is a real, in-scope security-relevant availability bug rather than a false positive. The main HTTP server exposes normal S3 multipart operations, and the storage code persists next_segment_vid on the primary during streaming UploadPart segment preparation before replicas necessarily apply AppendStreamSegment. CompleteMultipartUpload snapshots StreamUploadRecord values including next_segment_vid and CommitMultipartObject replica application requires exact equality. A replica lagging by one VID therefore rejects the command with a stream uploads mismatch. Earlier validation also exercised this path with a Rust unit-test PoC and LLDB breakpoint, showing primary next_segment_vid=2 versus replica next_segment_vid=1 and the real apply_commit_multipart_object_command mismatch branch. Severity remains medium: the effect can be persistent availability loss for the affected bucket/placement group, but it requires authenticated write access, a timing race, and does not expose data, bypass auth, execute code, or escalate privileges.
## Controls
- AWS SigV4 request authentication for normal private S3 operations
- Bucket/object authorization checks before streaming UploadPart and CompleteMultipartUpload
- Default listener is localhost-only at 127.0.0.1:9000 unless ARGMIN_LISTEN_ADDR is changed
- Optional direct TLS via ARGMIN_TLS_CERT_PATH and ARGMIN_TLS_KEY_PATH
- Connection and in-flight request semaphores plus timeouts in the HTTP server
- No executable sink involved; impact is metadata availability
## Blindspots
- Static repository artifacts did not include deployment manifests, so public versus internal exposure cannot be proven beyond the default localhost listener and configurable ARGMIN_LISTEN_ADDR.
- The prior PoC exercised the storage command path with unit-test-created primary/replica stores rather than a full end-to-end HTTP race harness.
- The exact blast radius of a wedged pending command may depend on placement-group topology, acting-set size, and operational recovery tooling not fully represented in static code.
- No cloud APIs were called and no live deployment configuration was inspected.
